#---
# purpose: "a receive guard orders a float the way a body does"
# oracle: oracle.exs
# defer: "the receive matcher compares guard operands as integers and refuses a float"
#---
#
# # receive_guard_float
#
# `x when x > 1.5` means the same thing in a receive clause as in a function
# head or an expression: the total term order, where a float and an integer
# compare by value. The message here is a float, so the first clause is the one
# that answers, on every door.
def main() do
  send(self(), 2.5)
  receive do
    x when x > 1.5 -> dbg(:big)
    x -> dbg({:small, x})
  end
end
